      "content": "hey, i need some quick advice. our company is getting absolutely hammered on twitter right now because we haven't released a statement on the new [Global Climate Equity Act] legislation. our core customers are calling us out for being \"silent\" and basically saying we don't care about the planet. \n\nwe're stuck between issuing a full endorsement of the act to quiet the backlash or just staying neutral to avoid pissing off our more conservative stakeholders. given the current PR climate, what do you think is the move here? should we just take a stand to protect the brand?",
